# Detections

Reusable Wazuh custom rules and a tiny test harness. Each rule lives in its
own file with a header comment containing:

- Rule ID
- ATT&CK technique(s)
- Author + date
- False-positive notes
- Reference

## Layout

```
detections/
├── README.md
├── local_rules.xml         ← combined ruleset ready to drop into Wazuh
└── tests/
    └── README.md           ← how to replay attacks against a rule
```

## Authoring rule

A new rule must include a `<mitre>` block and a header comment:

```xml
<!--
  id:    100101
  att&ck: T1548.003 Sudoers modification
  author: <you> 2026-07-26
  fp:     none observed during lab 04 testing
  ref:    labs/lab-04-detection-engineering
-->
<rule id="100101" level="12">
  ...
</rule>
```

## Deploy

```bash
sudo cp local_rules.xml /var/ossec/etc/rules/
sudo systemctl restart wazuh-manager
```

## Tests

For each rule, record the Atomic Red Team / custom command that triggers it
under `tests/` so a reviewer can reproduce the alert.
